## Holiday fun with real cultural learning

Our vacation care incursions are designed for school-aged children from 5 years old. They are fast-paced and full of movement, so children spend the session smiling, laughing, jumping and moving.

What’s more, our experienced facilitators share real stories from their own time in Africa and with African people. As a result, children don’t just play music. Instead, they discover the culture behind it.

### Learn, play and dance the rhythms of West Africa

During each program, children learn about African instruments and how they are made. Then they play the African drums and dance to the rhythms of West Africa. Finally, everyone comes together as one big, energetic ensemble.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
![School-aged children playing djembe drums together during vacation care incursions](/media/2018/09/A08R7271-e1550205581543.webp)
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

*Choose your program*

## Five vacation care incursions to choose from

There are five different vacation care incursions to choose from, so you can book something new each holiday. In addition, multiple bookings receive a package discount, which makes it easy to plan the whole year.

{% columns layout="equal" align="top" %}
{% column %}
### African drumming

Children play real djembes and learn traditional West African rhythms, as well as rhythm games and call-and-response.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Singing & call-and-response

Lively African songs and chants also build listening, memory and confidence, so every voice becomes part of the rhythm.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### African dance

Fun, energetic moves and movement games develop coordination and balance. They also get everyone up and moving.
{% /column %}

{% column %}
### Stories & instruments

Children hear real stories from Africa. They also discover where each instrument comes from and how it is made.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}

For a full overview of what we include in each session, see our [Drum Sing Dance Program](/drum-sing-dance-program/).

